# SEO

Reuse Next.js Metadata API on App Router pages. Do not add a second SEO stack. `useSEO` / `use-dynamic-title` are client helpers — prefer `export const metadata` (or `generateMetadata`) on pages.

## Brand and titles

- Product name in new/updated metadata: **Smart Tools**
- **ToolifyLab** only as project/company/publisher when that relationship is accurate
- Do not mass-rewrite existing titles unless the task is SEO/branding
- Root template in `layout.tsx` is `%s - ToolifyLab`. If you change brand suffix, update `title.template` together so titles do not become `Smart Tools - ToolifyLab`
- Prefer unique tool titles: `EMI Calculator`, `GST Calculator` (template appends brand). Target style when updating the template: `EMI Calculator | Smart Tools`
- 404 stays `robots: { index: false, follow: false }`

## Canonical and indexing

- Canonical domain: `process.env.SITE_URL` with fallback `https://tools.praveensingh.online` (matches `layout.tsx`)
- Do not invent a third domain. `next-sitemap.config.js` currently falls back to `tools.praveenskg.in` — do not “fix” that unless asked
- Reuse `alternates.canonical`, `metadataBase`, existing `robots` / `next-sitemap` (`postbuild`). Keep `/api/*` out of the sitemap
- No hosting-provider branding in user-facing metadata
- Preserve index/follow unless explicitly changing indexing

## Content

- Unique title + description per tool. No keyword stuffing, hidden SEO text, or duplicate canonical/schema
- Keywords: short, relevant; do not dump the whole catalog on every page
- Open Graph / Twitter: reuse `/og-image.png` or existing `/og/{tool}.png` paths; `siteName` consistent with the chosen product name
- Structured data: homepage already has `WebSite` + `ItemList`. `generateToolStructuredData` in `use-seo.ts` is `WebApplication`. Add Organization/WebSite only when accurate
- Never invent reviews, ratings, social profiles, addresses, or organization details. Publisher/author already used: ToolifyLab / Praveen Singh — do not fabricate extras
